[BLAME] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: In DAGRunner.run around lines 522-525, despite the author's CHANGE attempt to eliminate what was presumed to be a dead empty wave check, the implementation violates the contract in low/dag_engine_lite_impl.pyi which explicitly requires in DAGRunner.run grounding: 'Halts wave loop when next wave is empty.' When scheduler.is_finished() evaluates to False but scheduler.next_wave() yields an empty list (for example, when non-terminal nodes remain in RUNNING state or cannot be scheduled), omitting the break condition on an empty wave causes the while loop in DAGRunner.run to hang indefinitely in an infinite loop without forward progress. The runner must halt the wave loop whenever next_wave() returns an empty sequence.
